From: sbe1v1k 25.12-6.18 port <noreply@sbe1v1k-build>
Subject: [PATCH] qca-nss-sfe: use timer_delete() for 6.18

6.18 removed del_timer() with no compatibility alias; include/linux/timer.h
now declares timer_delete() with the same semantics. sfe_ipv6_frag_exit()
still tears down the per-CPU exception timers and the fragment timer with
the old name.

Rename both call sites; the timers are being freed right after, so the
delete-if-pending behaviour of del_timer() is what is kept.

Classification: portability (kernel API rename, same semantics).
--- a/sfe_ipv6_frag.c
+++ b/sfe_ipv6_frag.c
@@ -1276,14 +1276,14 @@
 	 */
 	for_each_online_cpu(cpu) {
 		struct sfe_ipv6_frag_exception *pcpu = per_cpu_ptr(sif->pcpu, cpu);
-		del_timer(&pcpu->timer);
+		timer_delete(&pcpu->timer);
 		skb_queue_purge(&pcpu->exception_queue);
 	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Delete the timer.
 	 */
-	del_timer(&sif->timer);
+	timer_delete(&sif->timer);
 
 	/*
 	 * Free the fragment entries.
